 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 383 of the laws of 1991, relating to the incorporation of the New York Zoological Society, in relation to extending the expiration date of free one day admission to the zoological park",
    "basePrintNo": "S6588",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6588-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 383 of 1991",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6588\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 383 of the laws of 1991, relating to the incorporation\nof the New York Zoological Society, in relation to extending the\nexpiration date of free one day admission to the zoological park\n\nPURPOSE:\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the expiration date of\nthe one day free admission policy of the zoological park of the New\nYork Zoological Society (the Bronx Zoo) for an additional three years.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1: Amends section 3 of Chapter 383 of the Laws of 1991, that\nrelates to the incorporation of the New York Zoological Society, to\ncontinue to reserve at least one day in each week as a free admission\nday for the general public, subject to such rules and regulations as\nthe corporation may prescribe.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nChapter 49 of the Laws of 2009 expires July 1, 2012.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation was initially signed into law as\nChapter 77 of the Laws of 2000. This bill extends the provisions of\nChapter 77 which extends the one-day free admission policy per week\nfor another three years. The Zoo will be able to maintain a viable\nfiscal position and provide the necessary means required to operate\nthis world class facility. In addition, the Zoo will be able to\nmaintain its educational programs for school children and continue to\nprovide its patrons with one free admission day. Zoo attendance over\nthe last three years, while the one-day free admission was in effect,\nhas increased overall.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire\nJuly 1, 2015.\n\n",
